  "verifiedAt": "2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z",
  "intro": "An antiderivative of $f$ is a function $F$ with $F'=f$. The indefinite integral collects all of them: $\\int f(x)\\,dx=F(x)+C$. Key rules: power rule for integrals $\\int x^n\\,dx=\\frac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}+C$ (for $n\\ne -1$), $\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,dx=\\ln|x|+C$, $\\int e^x\\,dx=e^x+C$, $\\int \\cos x\\,dx=\\sin x+C$, $\\int \\sin x\\,dx=-\\cos x+C$. Always include the constant $C$ for an indefinite integral.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "Find $\\int (6x^2-4x+5)\\,dx$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Integrate term by term with the power rule.",
          "$\\int 6x^2\\,dx=2x^3$, $\\int -4x\\,dx=-2x^2$, $\\int 5\\,dx=5x$.",
          "Add the constant: $2x^3-2x^2+5x+C$."
        ],
        "answer": "$2x^3-2x^2+5x+C$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "Find $\\int \\left(\\sqrt{x}+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\,dx$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Rewrite $\\sqrt{x}=x^{1/2}$.",
          "$\\int x^{1/2}\\,dx=\\frac{2}{3}x^{3/2}$ and $\\int\\frac{1}{x}\\,dx=\\ln|x|$.",
          "Combine: $\\frac{2}{3}x^{3/2}+\\ln|x|+C$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\dfrac{2}{3}x^{3/2}+\\ln|x|+C$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "Solve the initial value problem $F'(x)=3x^2$ with $F(1)=5$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Antiderivative: $F(x)=x^3+C$.",
          "Apply $F(1)=5$: $1+C=5$, so $C=4$.",
          "Thus $F(x)=x^3+4$."
        ],
        "answer": "$F(x)=x^3+4$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 4,
      "prompt": "Find $\\int (4x^3-2)\\,dx$.",
